NOTE — THIS LOG IS NOT THE OUTPUT OF THE COMMITTED verify.sh.
It is the output of an EARLIER draft of that script, retained as proof that the
harness is capable of failing. It reported 19 failed assertions and exited 19.
All 19 were defects in the CHECK, never in a finding:
  * S01-S21 failed because the draft computed the repository root one directory
    too shallow ("$(dirname "$0")/../../../../.." instead of six levels), so it
    read paths like <root>/research/docs/port/OWNER-REVIEW.md that do not exist.
  * S05-S08 were skipped because the draft looked for `uv` on PATH only, and uv
    lives at ~/.local/bin/uv on this host.
  * S63 and S73 failed because the draft expected the published manifests'
    [features] default arrays on one line; crates.io publishes them multi-line.
  * S99 failed because the draft compared the graph MSRV against "1.85" while
    hashbrown declares "1.85.0".
Each was fixed by changing the check. The committed script's own output is
r52-toml-crate.log, exit 0.
